{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_018NTopkXdkarEhnZTLf8yza","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils is a specification-driven development experiment that derives formal specs from GNU C source, generates Go implementations via an AI agent, and verifies output parity via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract, specify, synthesize, verify). Key components: `cmd/` (one package per utility), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `pkg/sys/` (syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `pkg/hashutil/` (shared hash functions), `docs/` (SRDs, use cases, test suites).\n\n**Current state**: This is generation run 44. Many utilities are implemented; the most recent work completed `cmd/printf` requirements R1.1-R1.4 (task 5480) and R2.1-R2.4 (task 5481). Printf still has R3.1-R3.4 and R4.1-R4.4 remaining. All of release 09.0 (sha224sum, sha384sum, b2sum, cksum, sum) is unstarted with all requirements ready.\n\n**Current release**: Release 08.1 is the earliest incomplete release with ready requirements (srd073-printf R3/R4). After that, release 09.0 (hash/checksum utilities).\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\n1. **Release 08.1** -- printf has 8 remaining ready requirements (R3.1-R3.4, R4.1-R4.4). Two tasks to complete it.\n2. **Release 09.0** -- sha224sum (srd074) has 12 ready requirements. Start with R1.1-R1.4 and R2.1-R2.3 (two tasks).\n\nEarlier incomplete releases (00.0 format/testutils, 01.1 cat, etc.) have no requirements in `requirement_states`, so they cannot be proposed.\n\n## Weight Budget Checks\n\nAssuming default weight 1 per requirement (no requirements.yaml available to read per tool constraints):\n\n- Task 0: cmd/printf R3.1 (w=1), R3.2 (w=1), R3.3 (w=1), R3.4 (w=1) → total 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n- Task 1: cmd/printf R4.1 (w=1), R4.2 (w=1), R4.3 (w=1), R4.4 (w=1) → total 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n- Task 2: cmd/sha224sum R1.1 (w=1), R1.2 (w=1), R1.3 (w=1), R1.4 (w=1) → total 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n- Task 3: cmd/sha224sum R2.1 (w=1), R2.2 (w=1), R2.3 (w=1) → total 3 ≤ 4 ✓\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/printf: srd073 R3.1-R3.4\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd073-printf.yaml (SRD for printf -- read requirements R3.1 through R3.4)\n      - cmd/printf/main.go (existing implementation covering R1.1-R2.4 -- extend with R3 requirements)\n      - cmd/printf/printf_test.go (existing differential tests -- add tests for R3 requirements)\n      - pkg/testutils/ (differential testing harness used by all cmd/ tests)\n      - pkg/sys/ (SIGPIPE handler -- already called in main, no changes needed)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/printf/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add functionality specified by srd073 R3.1-R3.4\n      - path: cmd/printf/printf_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add differential test cases for R3.1-R3.4\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement srd073-printf requirement R3.1 as specified in the SRD\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement srd073-printf requirement R3.2 as specified in the SRD\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement srd073-printf requirement R3.3 as specified in the SRD\n      - id: R4\n        text: Implement srd073-printf requirement R3.4 as specified in the SRD\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Extend the existing cmd/printf implementation -- do not rewrite or reorganize existing code that covers R1 and R2\n      - id: D2\n        text: Use the established differential testing pattern with testutils.RunDiffTests comparing against gprintf reference binary\n      - id: D3\n        text: Derive all implementation details from srd073-printf.yaml -- do not invent behavior not specified in the SRD\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: All four requirements R3.1-R3.4 from srd073-printf are implemented in cmd/printf/main.go\n      - id: AC2\n        text: Differential tests added to cmd/printf/printf_test.go for each R3 requirement\n      - id: AC3\n        text: go build ./cmd/printf/ succeeds with no errors\n      - id: AC4\n        text: go test ./cmd/printf/... -count=1 passes (skips gracefully if gprintf not in PATH)\n      - id: AC5\n        text: go vet ./cmd/printf/ reports no issues\n\n- index: 1\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/printf: srd073 R4.1-R4.4\"\n  dependency: 0\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd073-printf.yaml (SRD for printf -- read requirements R4.1 through R4.4)\n      - cmd/printf/main.go (existing implementation covering R1.1-R3.4 -- extend with R4 requirements)\n      - cmd/printf/printf_test.go (existing differential tests -- add tests for R4 requirements)\n      - pkg/testutils/ (differential testing harness used by all cmd/ tests)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/printf/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add functionality specified by srd073 R4.1-R4.4\n      - path: cmd/printf/printf_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add differential test cases for R4.1-R4.4\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement srd073-printf requirement R4.1 as specified in the SRD\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement srd073-printf requirement R4.2 as specified in the SRD\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement srd073-printf requirement R4.3 as specified in the SRD\n      - id: R4\n        text: Implement srd073-printf requirement R4.4 as specified in the SRD\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Extend the existing cmd/printf implementation -- do not rewrite or reorganize existing code that covers R1 through R3\n      - id: D2\n        text: Use the established differential testing pattern with testutils.RunDiffTests comparing against gprintf reference binary\n   